      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 5.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.01,
      "end_seconds": 10.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Okay, of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.23,
      "end_seconds": 18.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "it's severe tummy pain out of proportion to the examination, mostly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.05,
      "end_seconds": 22.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.2,
      "end_seconds": 32.43,
      "duration_seconds": 9.23,
      "text": "Maybe a three out of ten on a bad day. I'd been feeling very unwell, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.49,
      "end_seconds": 38.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.52,
      "end_seconds": 41.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "no allergies at all"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.02,
      "end_seconds": 44.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.21,
      "end_seconds": 47.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "No, never."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.71,
      "end_seconds": 64.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.79,
      "end_seconds": 78.04,
      "duration_seconds": 13.25,
      "text": "I have an irregular heartbeat. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.44,
      "end_seconds": 80.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.55,
      "end_seconds": 86.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "I've had diabetes for nearly five years now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.28,
      "end_seconds": 92.24,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.07,
      "end_seconds": 101.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well. Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.16,
      "end_seconds": 107.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.88,
      "end_seconds": 125.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.7,
      "end_seconds": 144.06,
      "duration_seconds": 17.36,
      "text": "I quit smoking around ten years ago. I only drink at family occasions. I live with my elderly mother. I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.27,
      "end_seconds": 152.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Any chest pain or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.93,
      "end_seconds": 157.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.91,
      "text": "Let me think, no, no chest pain or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.47,
      "end_seconds": 161.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "And hernia, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.41,
      "end_seconds": 163.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Definitely no hernia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.92,
      "end_seconds": 167.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.46,
      "end_seconds": 170.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.93,
      "end_seconds": 189.47,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Okay, I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.42,
      "end_seconds": 200.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.23,
      "end_seconds": 222.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 116 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pressure 125 over 81. And respiratory rate 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.06,
      "end_seconds": 226.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.87,
      "end_seconds": 230.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "they help me see the whole picture, more shortly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.99,
      "end_seconds": 237.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.32,
      "end_seconds": 240.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.87,
      "end_seconds": 266.96,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Your pulse is irregular, the tummy is soft but terribly painful, and the pain is out of proportion to what I find."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.77,
      "end_seconds": 269.7,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.63,
      "end_seconds": 313.66,
      "duration_seconds": 38.03,
      "text": "you can sit up now. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like possible bowel ischaemia. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out pancreatitis yet. Let's book an urgent CT angiogram to look into possible bowel ischaemia. Let's book urgent blood tests to look into severe abdominal pain. This is an emergency, you are going to hospital now. Book a a review straight away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.48,
      "end_seconds": 318.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.58,
      "end_seconds": 322.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "No, that's all. Thanks a lot."
    }
  ]
}